> The bastards keep multiplying.  I can't kill them.  I'm wearing a ring
> of conflict but it isn't working fast enough.  What can I do?

Wearing a ring of conflict is exactly the worst thing you can do in
that situation. Bear in mind that when a monster such as a gremlin
clones itself, the original's max HP are divided between the two
resulting monsters; thus, a finite number of starting gremlins will
result in a finite (if large) number of consequent gremlins with 1 HP
each. If you let them start killing each other, they'll be gaining
more HP (the monster equivalent of experience) to breed with, and can
keep that up until the entire level is full.

(This analysis isn't quite accurate, since there will be other beasties
being conflicted against the gremlins as well; however, they're unlikely
to make a significant impact on the population growth.)

The simplest solution is genocide. Alternatively, remove conflict, get
a beefy pet that can navigate over water, and let it munch its way
through the horde; or just give up on navigating the level and dig
down past it, planning on using cursed gain level to leave it on the
way up.

